# Shop Inventory & Sales API

A REST API for a small shop, built with Django and Django REST Framework. It tracks products and stock, records sales, and gives the owner a daily sales summary.

## Features
- Products and categories (full CRUD)
- Recording a sale automatically reduces stock
- Overselling protection: a sale fails if there isn't enough stock
- Token authentication with two roles:
  - **Owner** (staff): manages everything and sees the daily summary
  - **Cashier**: views products and records sales only
- Daily sales summary (owner only)

## Tech
Python, Django, Django REST Framework, SQLite

## Run it locally
```bash
git clone https://github.com/sumi74/shop-inventory-api.git
cd shop-inventory-api
python -m venv venv
venv\Scripts\activate        # Mac/Linux: source venv/bin/activate
pip install django djangorestframework
python manage.py migrate
python manage.py createsuperuser
python manage.py runserver
```

## Endpoints
| Method | Endpoint | Who | Purpose |
|---|---|---|---|
| POST | `/api/login/` | Anyone | Get an auth token |
| GET | `/api/products/` | Logged in | List products |
| POST/PUT/DELETE | `/api/products/` | Owner | Manage products |
| GET/POST | `/api/categories/` | Owner can edit | Manage categories |
| GET/POST | `/api/sales/` | Logged in | View / record sales |
| GET | `/api/sales/summary/` | Owner | Today's sales total |

## Example: record a sale
```json
POST /api/sales/
{"items": [{"product": 1, "quantity": 2}]}
```
Stock is reduced automatically, and the sale total is calculated.